# LEAPWare ShellUX - install policy that travels with the clone.
#
# Anything set here applies to every laptop that clones this repository. npm's own
# config is per-user and per-machine and does not travel, which is exactly the
# class of local-environment dependency ADR-0002 forbids.
#
# This file holds policy only. No credential, token or registry authentication
# belongs in a tracked file.

# Turn the `engines` floor in package.json from a warning into a hard failure.
#
# Without this, npm's default is to print EBADENGINE and carry on installing. A
# laptop on a Node below the floor then gets a tree that resolves but misbehaves
# later, somewhere unrelated and much harder to diagnose. The floor is derived
# from the transitive `engines` data in package-lock.json; see README.md
# "Prerequisites" for the reasoning and the exact constraints behind it.
engine-strict=true
